# Cloudflare Pages headers (copied verbatim into dist/ from public/).
#
# Cross-origin isolation is REQUIRED for stockfish.wasm's threaded build
# (SharedArrayBuffer needs document.crossOriginIsolated). Same pair the dev +
# preview servers set in vite.config.ts. Article 11: if a host omits these,
# the engine load rejects and the Coach degrades to "engine unavailable" — the
# trainer itself still works.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# Hashed build assets are content-addressed → cache forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Sidecars are regenerated per build but unhashed; revalidate.
/features.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/transpositions.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
/catalog.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# KNOWN ISSUE (free WebGPU tier): under COEP require-corp, the MLC model
# download from the cross-origin CDN may be blocked unless that CDN sends a
# Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy header. BYOK-cloud and Ollama tiers are
# unaffected. Resolve at the WebGPU hardening step — options: COEP
# `credentialless` (Chrome/FF), self-host the model weights same-origin, or
# gate the WebGPU tier behind a relaxed-header route.
